WEBVTT

00:05.140 --> 00:07.320
ECM online.
Activating evasive maneuver.

00:10.940 --> 00:12.150
I can't shake them off!

00:13.310 --> 00:14.790
Brace for impact!

00:27.720 --> 00:30.760
METALLIC ROUGE

02:09.720 --> 02:11.070
Morning, Sylvia.

02:12.200 --> 02:13.740
Sylvia.

02:13.740 --> 02:14.380
Yes.

02:14.870 --> 02:17.740
That is your name,
shining in the silvery white.

02:20.240 --> 02:21.710
Happy birthday.

02:25.920 --> 02:27.240
Birthday...

02:28.580 --> 02:30.490
You have been born just now.

02:30.920 --> 02:33.030
This is your world.

02:34.390 --> 02:35.530
Our...

02:36.410 --> 02:37.550
...world...

02:38.620 --> 02:41.280
Thank you for being born
into this world.

02:48.620 --> 02:49.940
That colour in your eyes...

02:51.130 --> 02:52.410
Just like Eva.

02:53.830 --> 02:57.760
The Crimson Princess is soon to arrive.

02:59.490 --> 03:03.660
I have welcomed Lady Rouge
and her friends as requested.

03:04.270 --> 03:06.870
I am sure you have made no slip, Opera.

03:07.220 --> 03:09.420
In order for them to safely arrive here,

03:09.820 --> 03:13.840
while a bit rough,
I have exercised discretion.

03:14.440 --> 03:16.440
You have heard her.

03:17.190 --> 03:19.600
The beginning of a new world.

03:24.120 --> 03:26.390
Angle of entry is 27!
We're too deep!

03:26.390 --> 03:28.100
Just break through like this now!

03:28.100 --> 03:28.980
Huh?!

04:03.580 --> 04:05.110
They have arrived.

04:06.150 --> 04:08.410
Gosh, what a rough ride...

04:08.410 --> 04:11.400
We can enter the plantation
from the maintenance hatch.

04:11.810 --> 04:15.370
Judging from where
the Puppeteer's ship is moored.

04:15.370 --> 04:16.839
Is my brother there?

04:17.160 --> 04:17.899
Let's hurry.

04:18.240 --> 04:22.070
The Altar and the Puppeteer
must know we're here.

04:22.390 --> 04:24.030
It's dangerous to stay put.

04:24.700 --> 04:25.510
Right...

04:27.020 --> 04:28.960
What about this kid?

04:29.290 --> 04:30.740
We'll take her with us.

04:31.210 --> 04:32.340
She's my family.

04:33.080 --> 04:34.380
Will she be okay?

04:34.730 --> 04:37.400
Even if I hear the voice,
I'll decide for myself.

04:48.540 --> 04:49.550
Noir...

04:50.720 --> 04:52.210
Be sure to greet him warmly.

04:54.730 --> 04:56.680
A new world is about to be born.

04:57.290 --> 04:58.990
Our world...

04:59.800 --> 05:01.260
Your world...

05:01.970 --> 05:03.230
That's what you said.

05:03.810 --> 05:07.040
And you also mentioned
I have a role in that world.

05:07.380 --> 05:08.780
Yes, you do.

05:09.290 --> 05:13.240
Your role will be given in time.

05:13.720 --> 05:17.700
Especially, since you are
the son of Eva Christella,

05:17.700 --> 05:21.430
you are obliged to fulfill that, no?

05:22.070 --> 05:23.760
What do you know about my mother?

05:24.230 --> 05:26.120
I was there as well.

05:26.120 --> 05:30.070
In the Nean development team
led by Professor Yunghart.

05:30.070 --> 05:34.860
Hence, I know a lot about your mother.

05:35.190 --> 05:40.380
Being the greatest assistant that's
ever lived to Professor Roy Yunghart,

05:40.380 --> 05:43.640
she left a glimpse of hope to the Neans.

05:43.640 --> 05:46.870
That is Code Eve.

05:49.130 --> 05:54.930
Then, she embedded that code deep inside
the bodies of the nine Neans.

05:56.130 --> 06:01.170
So that the Neans may someday
extract and obtain freedom from it.

06:01.560 --> 06:04.800
What a sign of affection indeed.

06:05.260 --> 06:12.250
Still, that affection greatly
turned her life into chaos.

06:15.230 --> 06:17.880
Eva Christella suddenly...

06:18.330 --> 06:21.280
...disappeared from those she knew...

06:21.280 --> 06:23.700
...without a trace.

06:24.320 --> 06:27.320
There was a secret
behind her disappearance.

06:27.320 --> 06:31.590
The thoughts one
could not convey to anyone...

06:31.590 --> 06:33.960
The secret love.

06:35.790 --> 06:41.260
And who could this secret
love of hers be, then?

06:41.940 --> 06:44.260
One with a loving family?

06:44.770 --> 06:46.870
One with a different status?

06:47.280 --> 06:52.520
He might not be a human...

06:54.140 --> 06:57.610
Jean, Jean, my beloved son...

06:57.610 --> 07:00.040
I shall tell you right now.

07:00.040 --> 07:03.900
Your real father is...

07:04.330 --> 07:05.910
Cut it out already.

07:06.710 --> 07:08.710
It was getting interesting, though.

07:08.710 --> 07:10.520
What a terrible skit.

07:11.400 --> 07:12.910
Is it?

07:14.880 --> 07:17.280
This world is but a stage.

07:17.680 --> 07:22.170
Just like a puppet show,
controlled by the unseen hands.

07:22.470 --> 07:26.880
Your mother was trying
to cut the threads,

07:26.880 --> 07:28.750
the Azimov Code,
controlling the Neans.

07:29.390 --> 07:33.960
For that, she gave birth
to Rouge Redstar,

07:33.960 --> 07:38.110
with the final key to deciphering it,
which is Code Eve, embedded and sealed.

07:38.780 --> 07:43.030
However, you, as her son, used Rouge,

07:43.030 --> 07:47.030
and tried to cover up the Immortal Nine.

07:47.670 --> 07:48.660
I won't deny that.

07:48.950 --> 07:50.730
But why?

07:51.240 --> 07:54.140
Had you talked with us,
we would have...

07:54.140 --> 07:54.940
I did.

07:54.940 --> 07:55.660
Huh?

07:56.290 --> 07:57.160
I have...

07:57.840 --> 07:59.000
...talked with him.

08:00.660 --> 08:05.050
Jean said he had begun working
on the coexistence between humans and Neans.

08:05.740 --> 08:08.100
That was his reason
for joining the Ministry.

08:08.710 --> 08:12.120
But I can't trust humans.

08:13.060 --> 08:17.670
The corrupt bureaucracy will
eventually swallow his idealism,

08:17.670 --> 08:19.630
and crush it to the bone.

08:20.220 --> 08:21.110
Also...

08:21.810 --> 08:24.360
You said you didn't have time to wait.

08:25.670 --> 08:27.490
And you killed Father.

08:27.850 --> 08:30.740
Sylvia did...?

08:31.640 --> 08:35.080
Yung knew too much about us.

08:35.350 --> 08:40.480
And with that,
I was asked to be the watchman.

08:40.480 --> 08:45.220
But you wouldn't ask me
to simply watch over, would you?

08:47.750 --> 08:50.750
We lost connection with Venus.

08:51.330 --> 08:56.680
We believe the Altar has taken over
the whole plantation system.

08:57.130 --> 08:59.640
How is the fleet doing right now?

08:59.950 --> 09:03.400
The main fleet in the asteroid belt
is rendered immobile now.

09:03.710 --> 09:08.280
However, the Sixth Space Corps
on the Moon would be deployable.

09:08.540 --> 09:11.720
Hold on, if by attacking,

09:11.720 --> 09:15.110
we stop, or worse,
destroy, the black reactor,

09:15.110 --> 09:17.080
containing the micro black hole...

09:17.530 --> 09:19.630
The whole Venus will be destroyed,

09:19.630 --> 09:23.460
or in the best-case scenario,
it will deviate from its current orbit.

09:25.500 --> 09:28.460
This may be inevitable, I'm afraid.

09:29.080 --> 09:32.980
Fortunately,
our agents are on Venus now.

09:32.980 --> 09:35.010
They are on a mission
to stop the bogeys.

09:35.290 --> 09:36.100
Deputy Commander.

09:36.600 --> 09:39.100
Could we leave this to them now?

09:39.420 --> 09:44.230
I heard your former subordinate
Yunghart is on Venus as well.

09:45.610 --> 09:50.570
Yes, which is precisely
why the success rate will be high.

09:51.020 --> 09:54.280
How many times have we tagged
along with your cajolery now?

09:54.680 --> 09:56.440
I lost count already.

09:57.130 --> 10:01.120
But your cajolery is always a good one.

10:07.550 --> 10:10.010
#11 TARGET PLANET

10:12.070 --> 10:16.090
The moving carnival is berthing on Dock 3C.

10:16.450 --> 10:18.900
We can access Dock A from both wings.

10:20.540 --> 10:22.030
Which route is the best?

10:22.410 --> 10:25.720
Preferably the shortest one
with the least security.

10:26.070 --> 10:28.270
Tread lightly, and keep the pace...

10:28.270 --> 10:29.960
Hey, I was speaking here!

10:29.960 --> 10:30.650
Hey!

10:33.960 --> 10:34.860
Ash, Cyan!

10:42.730 --> 10:43.910
Drat!

10:45.340 --> 10:47.180
We can regroup at the carnival ship.

10:47.180 --> 10:48.360
Aye.

10:49.190 --> 10:50.260
Where's Sis?

10:51.510 --> 10:56.000
Let's go, Cyan. It's a race to
the finish against Rouge now.

10:58.010 --> 10:59.760
Got it!

10:59.760 --> 11:01.350
Ready... Go!

11:09.270 --> 11:13.820
They are now separated,
as requested.

11:14.190 --> 11:16.700
The west wing has Lady Rouge
and the DoD lady.

11:17.500 --> 11:20.150
The east wing has the inspector
from the Protection Bureau,

11:20.150 --> 11:23.110
Cyan, and Master Jet Black Noir.

11:27.860 --> 11:29.830
I know you well.

11:30.570 --> 11:31.590
Have it your way.

11:33.310 --> 11:34.280
Thank you.

11:35.930 --> 11:40.500
So we're returning Noir's id
to have a fair fight, eh?

11:40.500 --> 11:42.770
Isn't this dramatic?

11:43.370 --> 11:45.110
I'm the same as Rouge.

11:45.570 --> 11:49.020
This hand has been
stained with my own kin's blood.

11:49.360 --> 11:52.830
Yet, you followed me
without saying anything.

11:53.470 --> 11:56.410
I shall return for you.

11:56.740 --> 11:58.300
For this world with you in it.

12:06.340 --> 12:09.110
On the west wing,
in Area B6,

12:09.110 --> 12:12.010
we have spotted Lady Rouge
and the DoD lady entering.

12:13.160 --> 12:14.050
Go.

12:14.690 --> 12:16.090
Kill the DoD girl.

12:16.090 --> 12:16.720
Wha...

12:18.870 --> 12:21.790
Anything you want to say
to your little sister?

12:22.600 --> 12:24.930
Kill the man before you.

12:26.120 --> 12:28.980
I'll tell her you love her.

12:38.860 --> 12:39.900
Rouge?

12:40.940 --> 12:44.310
Cyan... She really
should stick close to me.

12:45.530 --> 12:48.250
Our priority should be the carnival ship.

12:48.590 --> 12:52.250
But if I leave her alone,
she'll push herself too far!

12:52.690 --> 12:56.270
If she pushes herself too far,
her enemies will just get wrecked.

12:57.030 --> 12:57.960
She'd do that.

12:59.170 --> 12:59.990
You're right...

13:00.950 --> 13:05.370
I was made by the Visitors
to make the most logical decisions.

13:05.370 --> 13:08.270
My words are always right.

13:08.270 --> 13:09.730
So don't worry.

13:10.100 --> 13:12.310
All's well that ends well equals logical?

13:12.630 --> 13:14.610
We've come this far with that, no?

13:25.790 --> 13:27.920
Phew...

13:28.650 --> 13:30.250
Even if a new door...

13:30.750 --> 13:33.400
...were to open by Code Eve,

13:34.060 --> 13:38.550
not all Neans would come
to you like Graufon did.

13:39.380 --> 13:40.630
This planet...

13:41.070 --> 13:43.510
...has Nean and Nectar plantations...

13:43.510 --> 13:45.510
...to support the labour on it.

13:46.360 --> 13:48.540
A few years from now,

13:48.540 --> 13:51.850
the supplies needed to create
Neans will be stockpiled.

13:53.110 --> 13:55.400
Even if not all Neans are obedient,

13:55.930 --> 13:59.670
new comrades will be made
here to fight alongside us.

14:00.750 --> 14:04.030
That is proof of our existence.

14:04.410 --> 14:06.660
This isn't a world merely for humans.

14:07.130 --> 14:09.590
It is also one for us Neans.

14:10.730 --> 14:11.710
Hence...

14:12.070 --> 14:14.580
You're just benefiting
from the Usurpers.

14:14.880 --> 14:16.550
What do you call this?

14:16.910 --> 14:19.550
Profiting while others fight?
Sounds interesting.

14:20.260 --> 14:22.340
I'll make them regret it, then.

14:23.130 --> 14:26.010
Alcos, take him to his room.

14:26.310 --> 14:27.650
Me?

14:28.410 --> 14:29.320
Roger.

14:38.840 --> 14:40.650
When we're at the carnival ship,

14:40.650 --> 14:43.360
let's find the Code Eve analyser first.

14:44.230 --> 14:45.510
What about Jean?

14:46.920 --> 14:50.070
His wish is for us to stop Sylvia,

14:50.070 --> 14:52.700
and protect humans and Neans' freedom.

14:53.080 --> 14:54.560
I'll accomplish that.

14:55.270 --> 14:56.230
I see.

14:56.830 --> 14:58.420
Nice expression you have there.

14:58.690 --> 14:59.910
Why, thank you.

15:15.180 --> 15:16.410
Eva...

15:17.200 --> 15:19.900
Hey, you okay?

15:21.700 --> 15:25.180
Seems like I'll be seeing you sooner, Noid.

15:44.790 --> 15:47.270
I've decided for myself.

15:47.560 --> 15:49.470
I'll help Rouge with whatever I can.

15:49.900 --> 15:52.050
I'll protect Eden and you.

15:52.730 --> 15:54.890
You're my strangers, after all.

15:55.330 --> 15:56.020
Huh?

15:56.380 --> 15:58.220
Wait, did I say that wrong?

15:58.540 --> 15:59.870
You're a stranger something?

16:00.270 --> 16:01.770
I don't really get it,

16:02.390 --> 16:03.750
but I'm counting on you.

16:06.610 --> 16:09.350
Just one more spurt.

16:10.890 --> 16:12.160
Yeah.

16:23.480 --> 16:26.690
You were trying to discuss with us.

16:28.360 --> 16:29.410
At the lake...

16:30.010 --> 16:32.330
I remember catching bugs with you.

16:33.270 --> 16:35.220
There was a bug
we'd never seen before!

16:36.080 --> 16:38.070
You were my family.

16:38.710 --> 16:43.340
Hence, I dreamed of a world
where humans and Neans could coexist.

16:44.910 --> 16:47.820
So, in order to make it come true,

16:47.820 --> 16:50.660
you ordered that girl
to kill her own kin?

16:53.190 --> 16:55.370
You and Sylvia are the same.

16:56.010 --> 17:00.790
Seems like a lot of people and Neans
turn dumb when thinking too much.

17:01.320 --> 17:02.510
I suppose so.

17:03.320 --> 17:05.690
There might actually be another way.

17:06.400 --> 17:09.930
But I don't hate such idiots.

17:17.140 --> 17:18.490
Cyan...

17:19.160 --> 17:21.880
O young girl, born at the Carnival.

17:22.730 --> 17:23.990
I hear the voice...

17:24.579 --> 17:26.640
You promised your sister, right?

17:26.640 --> 17:29.240
Decide for yourself
even if you hear it.

17:29.850 --> 17:31.410
Come, Cyan.

17:32.010 --> 17:33.810
Come to the Carnival.

17:36.240 --> 17:38.470
Don't give in to the voice!

17:38.470 --> 17:40.370
I must go...

17:40.370 --> 17:44.350
- I must go!
- Hang in there! You're stronger than this!

17:51.850 --> 17:52.600
Cyan!

17:54.450 --> 17:55.290
Cyan!

18:05.450 --> 18:07.270
Ash, stop Cyan.

18:08.690 --> 18:12.090
You're the only one
who can stop her.

18:12.090 --> 18:15.450
Also, he's only got beef with me, I think.

18:15.450 --> 18:17.070
Go, human.

18:17.070 --> 18:18.620
See you at the finish line.

18:36.480 --> 18:38.700
You are back, Cyan.

18:39.060 --> 18:42.230
My beloved daughter.

18:42.700 --> 18:44.280
Masked Dad...

18:44.800 --> 18:47.590
So that voice wasn't Dad...

18:48.930 --> 18:51.690
No, it was me.

18:52.280 --> 18:53.350
That guy...

19:02.920 --> 19:05.830
Now, for the final programme.

19:10.230 --> 19:11.670
Don't touch her!

19:12.390 --> 19:13.230
Hm?

19:14.230 --> 19:18.510
You are now playing a new role.

19:19.720 --> 19:23.480
A new stage... A new life...

19:23.750 --> 19:25.190
Now the curtain rises again.

19:25.910 --> 19:30.290
Me, of all people,
got bamboozled so bad...

19:40.210 --> 19:41.080
Damn!

19:51.840 --> 19:54.090
I wonder if Cyan and the others
are there yet...

19:54.470 --> 19:58.600
Either way,
we don't have time to wait around.

20:04.010 --> 20:04.660
This way.

20:08.070 --> 20:09.490
Where are we headed?

20:09.990 --> 20:12.710
The black reactor.
This way is quicker.

20:12.710 --> 20:14.040
Black?

20:14.040 --> 20:15.360
What's that?

20:16.090 --> 20:19.490
A power generator that uses
a small black hole, bit by bit.

20:19.920 --> 20:20.850
Let's haul ass!

20:20.850 --> 20:21.580
Okay.

20:22.870 --> 20:25.600
I really need to stop those guys.

20:26.850 --> 20:28.370
If I can't...

20:29.520 --> 20:30.790
I will...

20:32.040 --> 20:32.790
Rouge!

20:36.570 --> 20:37.670
So you're safe.

20:43.450 --> 20:46.080
So this is capriciousness...

20:47.280 --> 20:48.970
So unfathomable.

20:57.130 --> 20:58.700
Fret not.

20:58.970 --> 21:02.990
The unwanted son of yours is still alive.

21:04.490 --> 21:06.730
Return Jean at once.
